  "question": {
    "text": "A light ray is incident on the surface of a sphere of refractive index $n$ at an angle of incidence $\\theta_0$. The ray partially refracts into the sphere with angle of refraction $\\phi_0$ and then partly reflects from the back surface. The reflected ray then emerges out of the sphere after a partial refraction. The total angle of deviation of the emergent ray with respect to the incident ray is $\\alpha$. Match the quantities mentioned in List-I with their values in List-II and choose the correct option.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/O-k7gvvPw61P_L6mFG2e63UZ3dHfYTT572emfQecF6c.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bijwY",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 5 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 2 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 1 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GIU7h",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 5 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 1 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 2 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GZLEa",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 3 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 2 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 1 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7xicF",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 3 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 1 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 2 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/WdRJlTTfYBGD1DTRHkEZwUlBWuyvEM1rYezSWCjZZrY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>$\\begin{aligned} & \\alpha=\\left(\\theta_0-\\phi_0\\right)+\\left(180-2 \\phi_0\\right)+\\left(\\theta_0-2 \\phi_0\\right) \\\\ & \\alpha=180+2 \\theta_0-4 \\phi_0\\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\textbf{(P) } \\alpha=180+2 \\theta_0-4 \\phi_0$\r\n$180=180+2 \\theta_0-4 \\phi_0 \\Rightarrow \\theta_0=2 \\phi_0$ ...(i)\r\n$\\sin \\theta_0=2 \\sin \\phi_0$  ...(ii)\r\nFrom (i) & (ii)\r\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\sin \\theta_0=2 \\sin \\left(\\theta_0 / 2\\right) \\Rightarrow \\cos \\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)=1 \\\\ & \\frac{\\theta_0}{2}=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\theta_0=0\\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\textbf{(Q) } \\theta_0=2 \\phi_0$  ...(i)\r\n$\\sin \\theta_0=\\sqrt{3} \\sin \\phi_0$  ...(ii)\r\nFrom (i) & (ii)\r\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\sin \\theta_0=\\sqrt{3} \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\cos \\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ & \\frac{\\theta_0}{2}=30,150 \\\\ & \\theta_0=60,300 \\text { (Rejected) } \\\\ & \\theta_0=60 , 0\\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\textbf{(R) } \\theta_0=2 \\phi_0$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\sin \\theta_0=\\sqrt{3} \\sin \\phi_0 \\\\ & \\sin 2 \\theta_0=\\sqrt{3} \\sin \\phi_0 \\\\ & \\cos \\phi_0=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ & \\phi_0=30,150 \\text { (Rejected) }\\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\phi_0=30, 0$    ...(iii)\r\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\textbf {(S) } \\sin 45=\\sqrt{2} \\cos \\phi_0 \\\\ & \\cos \\phi_0=1 / 2 \\\\ & \\phi_0=60 \\\\ & \\alpha=180+2 \\theta_0-4 \\phi_0\\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\alpha=180+90-120$    ...(iv)\r\n$=180-30 ; \\alpha=150^{\\circ}$",
    "image": null
  },
